  "description": "Document 113 event contract for the events app/modules/yield_reconciliation/commands.py actually emits. 6 of the catalogue's 7 declared Document 17 events are implemented: YieldCalculated, YieldOutOfLimit (mutually exclusive on the same call site -- ternary on out_of_limit), MaterialReconciliationCalculated, ReconciliationFailed (mutually exclusive -- ternary on within-tolerance), YieldVerified, ReconciliationVerified (mutually exclusive -- ternary on cmd.record_kind). ReconciliationSuperseded is declared in 07_EVENT_CATALOGUE.yaml but has no producing code path -- superseding an already-verified reconciliation record is not yet built. Verified directly against source, not assumed. KNOWN DEFECT (SG-174, not fixed here): app/modules/material/commands.py also emits the literal event_type \"MaterialReconciliationCalculated\" (Document 22 material-level reconciliation, aggregate_type material_reconciliation) -- a second, independent cross-module name collision, same class as LineClearanceCompleted. See event-mat-002d.json.",
